Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 20:47:23 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 22/71] Default the TUI to the Z.ai provider

An unset model_provider resolved to OpenAI even though the default model is
served by Z.ai, so a fresh install opened on OpenAI's login screen and then
pointed at the wrong endpoint. Resolve the default in the TUI's config funnel
rather than in the loader, so the in-process harnesses that expect OpenAI's
wire format are untouched. An explicit model_provider still wins.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 codex-rs/tui/src/lib.rs | 32 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 31 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/codex-rs/tui/src/lib.rs b/codex-rs/tui/src/lib.rs
index d1043145ed..6bf2900f7f 100644
--- a/codex-rs/tui/src/lib.rs
+++ b/codex-rs/tui/src/lib.rs
@@ -55,6 +55,7 @@ use codex_login::default_client::originator;
 use codex_login::default_client::set_default_client_residency_requirement;
 use codex_login::enforce_login_restrictions;
 use codex_login::is_workload_identity_selected;
+use codex_model_provider_info::ZAI_PROVIDER_ID;
 use codex_protocol::ThreadId;
 use codex_protocol::auth::AuthMode;
